<p>You can see the contour points of the face, mouth, nose, eyes and eyebro=
ws were all marked by the points our algorithm found.</p>
<h1 id=3D"Landmarks:PerformingFaceRecognition-Conclusion">Conclusion</h1>
<p>In this article, we explored how to use the Vision Framework to detect k=
ey points on a face. We went through:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>How to set up and use</strong> <code>VNDetectFaceLandmarksReques=
t</code>, and what its parameters mean.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>How to draw the detected rectangles</strong> on the image using =
<code>CGContext</code> and convert coordinates with <code>VNImageRectForNor=
malizedRect</code></p></li>
</ul>
<p>Notice how the flow Request =E2=86=92 Handler =E2=86=92 Response is supe=
r similar to the previous examples. It shows how modular the Vision Framewo=
rk is and how easy it=E2=80=99s to use once you've got the pattern down.</p=
>
<p>You can go ahead and download this code, test it out, try it on differen=
t scenarios and even tweak it to display landmarks from a live camera feed.=
</p>
    </div>
</body>
